From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Greta Zhang <greta.zhang@mediatek.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 18:10:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: ASoC: SOF: mt8901: add ADSP power-management
 driver

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2166301

Bind the MT8901 audio DSP ACPI devices (NVDA8301, NVDA8302, NVDA8303)
and manage their power state through the power_wrap client interface:
runtime-PM suspend releases the DSP domain vote so the SoC can reach
its low-power states, resume reacquires it. Without a bound driver the
DSP domain stays powered and blocks the deepest platform sleep state.

No SOF core, firmware loading, IPC or topology is set up yet. This is
the power scaffold the SOF platform driver for the HiFi5 cores will
extend once the DSP firmware is available, and it lives under
sound/soc/sof/mediatek/mt8901 so that extension lands in place.

